# The statements of the finally block exist once, for both ways into them. The way without an exception carries a completion kind of 0 and its result as a boxed value into that block,
# branches on the kind behind it, and tests the boxed result for a number before it returns it.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="enter" role=Source
# CHECK: Double b@[[result]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}Terminal|ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: #[[next]], Rare:#[[handler]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[next]]:
# CHECK: Upsilon($0(b@{{*}}), ^[[kind]], WritesLocalState)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[kind]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[completion]] = Phi(
# CHECK: Store(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}Writes:ModuleVariables{{*}}:PutModuleVariable)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[kind]], Terminal)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:Rare:#{{*}}, Else:#[[returns]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[returns]]:
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[numberBits]] = BitAnd(b@[[completion]], {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[numberBits]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Return(b@[[completion]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The function has calls, and Windows passes arguments in other registers: its count is not checked.
# X64: instructions: 17, patchpoints: 3, rare instructions: 10
# ARM64 boxes the number in line, where x86-64 calls a stub.
# ARM64: instructions: 28, patchpoints: 3, rare instructions: 10
